/*!
\page page_stEmcCluster StEmcCluster

\brief Reconstructed cluster of adjacent hits in a STAR EMC sub-detector.

\section emccluster_overview Overview

StEmcCluster represents a group of neighbouring StEmcRawHit cells that share
energy from a common electromagnetic shower in one sub-detector of the STAR
Electromagnetic Calorimeter.  It stores the total energy, the (η, φ) centroid,
the RMS shower widths in η and φ, a list of constituent hits, adjacent
clusters, and matched tracks.

The class derives from StHit so that the sub-detector identity is encoded in
the inherited hardware-position word and the cluster can participate in
track–calorimeter matching.

\section emccluster_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StMeasuredPoint → StHit → StEmcCluster
\endcode

Clusters are stored in StEmcClusterCollection, which is attached to
\ref page_stEmcDetector "StEmcDetector".

\section emccluster_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Float_t | mEta | Pseudorapidity centroid of the cluster. |
| Float_t | mPhi | Azimuthal centroid [rad]. |
| Float_t | mSigmaEta | RMS η shower width. |
| Float_t | mSigmaPhi | RMS φ shower width [rad]. |
| Float_t | mEnergy | Total calibrated energy [GeV]. |
| StPtrVecEmcRawHit | mHits | Constituent raw hits (non-owning). |
| StPtrVecEmcCluster | mNeighbors | Adjacent clusters (non-owning). |
| StPtrVecTrack | mTracks | Matched reconstructed tracks (non-owning). |

\section emccluster_methods Key Methods

- \c eta(), \c phi() — cluster centroid.
- \c sigmaEta(), \c sigmaPhi() — RMS shower widths.
- \c energy() — total cluster energy [GeV].
- \c nHits(), \c hit() — constituent raw hits.
- \c nNeighbors(), \c neighbor() — adjacent clusters.
- \c nTracks(), \c track() — matched tracks.
- \c detector() — sub-detector ID (from StHit bit field).
- \c addHit(), \c addNeighbor(), \c addTrack() — population helpers.
- \c Print() — print summary to stdout.

\section emccluster_seealso See Also

\ref page_stEmcRawHit "StEmcRawHit",
\ref page_stEmcPoint "StEmcPoint",
\ref page_stEmcDetector "StEmcDetector"
*/
